==Hindi==
{{wikipedia|lang=hi|sc=Deva}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|hi}} {{term|ईश्वर|tr=īśvára|lang=sa}}. From {{etyl|sa|hi}} {{term|ईश्|ईश्|tr=īś|the supreme spirit, master, lord|lang=sa}} + {{term|वर|वर|tr=vára|most excellent or eminent among or for ; best|lang=sa}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/iːʃʋər/|lang=hi}}

===Noun===
{{hi-noun|g=m|tr=īśvar|ur=ایشور}} <ref>[http://spokensanskrit.de/index.php?script=HK&beginning=0+&tinput=+%E0%A4%88%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%B0&trans=Translate&direction=AU#Sanskrit|%E0%A4%88%E0%A4%B6%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%B5%E0%A4%B0 Ishvara in http://spokensanskrit.de]</ref>

# [[God]]
#: {{lang|hi|हम प्रतिदिन '''ईश्वर''' से प्रार्थना करते हैं।|}}
#: We pray to '''God''' everyday.
#: {{lang|hi|'''ईश्वर''' सब कुछ जानता है।|}}
#: '''God''' knows everything.
# [[Supreme]] [[Being]]
# [[supreme]] [[soul]]
# [[one]] of the [[रुद्र#Sanskrit|rudras]]
# [[ruler]], [[lord]], [[master]]

